id: recipe.file-processing-pipeline
kind: recipe
title: File processing pipeline
aliases: file pipeline, document ingest, batch file processing
question: how would you design a pipeline that processes uploaded files?
tags: architecture, batch, data
properties:
  - large payloads never in the message queue
  - bounded parallelism per stage
  - resumable per file
  - poison files quarantined, not blocking
invariant: Store the bytes durably, queue only references, process in bounded idempotent stages keyed by content digest.
answer_30s: Upload directly to object storage, enqueue the object key, process with a bounded worker pool in resumable stages recorded per file digest, and quarantine files that fail repeatedly.
flow: |
  client -> object storage (direct upload, pre-signed)
     |
  enqueue {key, digest, size}
     |
  queue -> stage workers (parse -> transform -> index)
     |
  per-file state: received/parsed/transformed/indexed (resumable)
     |
  failures: retry -> dead letter -> quarantine + alert
compose:
  - design.file-pipeline => the stage model and content-address idempotency
  - design.worker-pool => bounded concurrency sized to CPU or IO, not to arrivals
  - design.bounded-queue => backlog visible and bounded per stage
  - design.idempotency => reprocessing a file is free
  - design.state-machine => per-file status, so a stuck file is identifiable
  - design.backpressure => a slow stage slows ingestion instead of buffering
  - design.observability => per-stage throughput, queue depth, failure rate
  - k8s.deployment => stage workers scale independently
  - k8s.resources.limits => memory limits sized for the largest file a worker may parse
  - rust.bounded-concurrency => at most N files in flight in-process
  - rust.async-streams => stream the object rather than loading it whole
failure_modes:
  - file bytes through the queue payload, so the broker becomes storage
  - unbounded parallelism, so memory collapses on large inputs
  - no per-file state, so a restart reprocesses everything
  - one poison file blocking the partition (no quarantine path)
follow_ups:
  - how do you reprocess one file after fixing the parser?
related:
  - design.file-pipeline
  - design.worker-pool
  - k8s.job
sources:
  - https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/optimize-uploads.html
